Fix gensym.awk to emit a \n escape rather than a literal newline.

LITES generates .symc files containing

    asm ("
    * NAME mAgIc%0" : : "i" (expr));

A literal newline inside a string literal was accepted by K&R-era
compilers; modern C requires an escape, and gcc reports

    bsd_types_gen.symc:8:6: error: missing terminating " character

The assembly output is unchanged -- the newline still reaches the .s
file, it is just escaped in the C source. This is the same trick, and
the same modernisation, as OSFMK's own genassym.

Apply with:  patch -p1 -d /path/to/lites < gensym-newline.patch

--- a/conf/gensym.awk
+++ b/conf/gensym.awk
@@
-	print "asm (\"";
+	printf "asm (\"\\n";
